      "text": "To find \\( f(3) \\), we start with the given functional equation:\n\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2. \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2. \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\]\n\nNow we have a system of two equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27 \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12 \\)\n\nTo eliminate \\( f(-2) \\), we can multiply the first equation by 2 and then subtract the second equation from it:\n\n\\[ 2(f(3) + 2f(-2)) = 2 \\cdot 27 \\]\n\\[ 2f(3) + 4f(-2) = 54. \\]\n\nNow, we subtract the second equation from the first:\n\n\\[ (2f(3) + 4f(-2)) - (f(-2) + 2f(3)) = 54 - 12 \\]\n\\[ 2f(3) + 4f(-2) - f(-2) - 2f(3) = 42 \\]\n\\[ 3f(-2) = 42 \\]\n\\[ f(-2) = 14. \\]\n\nNow substitute \\( f(-2) = 14 \\) back into the first equation:\n\n\\[ f(3) + 2 \\cdot 14 = 27 \\]\n\\[ f(3) + 28 = 27 \\]\n\\[ f(3) = 27 - 28 \\]\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
