      "text": "To find \\( f(3) \\), we start with the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\nFirst, we substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3 \\cdot 3^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\tag{1} \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\tag{2} \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27 \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12 \\)\n\nTo eliminate \\( f(-2) \\), we can multiply the first equation by 2:\n\\[ 2f(3) + 4f(-2) = 54. \\tag{3} \\]\n\nNow we subtract the second equation from equation (3):\n\\[ (2f(3) + 4f(-2)) - (f(-2) + 2f(3)) = 54 - 12. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 3f(-2) = 42. \\]\nSolving for \\( f(-2) \\), we get:\n\\[ f(-2) = 14. \\]\n\nNow we substitute \\( f(-2) = 14 \\) back into equation (1):\n\\[ f(3) + 2 \\cdot 14 = 27. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 28 = 27. \\]\nSolving for \\( f(3) \\), we get:\n\\[ f(3) = 27 - 28 = -1. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
